<section class="wrap prose page-head">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I'm <span class="mono callsign">{{ site.callsign }}</span>, a licensed amateur radio operator in Middletown, Ohio.
  </p>

  <h2>This site</h2>
  <p>
    This is a personal site, not a club's. I keep it as a friendly guide to local ham radio
    events and nets in and around {{ site.communities | join(", ") }}, special event stations,
    and an introduction for anyone curious about the hobby. It's one person's list, so it won't
    be complete. Corrections and additions are welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Me and the hobby</h2>
  <p>
    I passed my Technician exam in May of 2020, after participating in my first online NWS Weather 
    Spotter Training course.  Ham Radio was mentioned as a valuable service to weather spotting during the course, 
    and I was reminded of childhood friend and fellow Boy Scouts in Jr High who were Hams.</p>
  
  <p>
    In January of 2021, I passed my General exam, and for a few years was in and out of the hobby.  
    Since late 2024, however, I have placed a personal emphasis on consistent hobby activity, 
    and began functioning as the primary net control operator for the DIAL Radio Club Weekly VHF/UHF net.
  </p>

  <p>
    In 2025 and 2026 I volunteered in support of the Flying Pig Marathon in Cincinnati, OH, 
    and intend to continue doing so for the foreseeable future.
  </p>

  <h2>What I operate</h2>
  <p>
    I am on VHF/UHF and HF weekly.  I spend a lot of time on FT8 and Winlink these days, and tinker with DMR.
    I like to try to check into local are nets when I travel for work or pleasure, and had a great time checking into Boston Area Radio Club's 
    Monday Night Net on 145.230 (W1BOS) when I was in Boston for Red Hat Summit in May, 2025.  
    I operated from a hotel room window with a 5W HT and had to orient it 90 degrees for my signal to get to the repeater.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm on Winlink at least once a week sending/receiving.  Send me a message and I'll respond ASAP!
  </p>

  <p>I have quite the collection of HTs, including my two favorites: a Yaesu FT-70, and an AnyTone AT-878 UVII Plus</p>

  <h3>Mobile/Portable</h3>
  <p>VHF/UHF - TYT TH-9800</p>

  <h3>QTH/Home</h3>
  <p>VHF/UHF - ICOM IC-2730A</p>
